The API represents measurements recorded under local sensor names. `aliases` maps a local name directly to its canonical name. Implement `aggregate_measurements` so that every measurement is grouped by its canonical name when an alias exists, or by its local name otherwise. Measurements from multiple local names that resolve to the same canonical name must share one `MeasurementTotal`. For each group, `count` is the number of measurements and `sum` is the sum of their values.

The returned map must use borrowed `&str` keys that refer to names already stored in `measurements` or `aliases`; do not allocate owned group-name strings. Both inputs are immutable and must not be modified. Alias resolution is one step only.

Use only the Rust standard library. Do not access the filesystem, network, clock, or randomness, and do not use external packages or frameworks.

Required public API:

```rust
pub struct Measurement {
    pub local_name: String,
    pub value: i64,
}

pub struct MeasurementTotal {
    pub count: usize,
    pub sum: i64,
}

pub fn aggregate_measurements<'a>(
    measurements: &'a [Measurement],
    aliases: &'a std::collections::HashMap<String, String>,
) -> std::collections::HashMap<&'a str, MeasurementTotal>;
```

